  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_1d82fd64055a4062925029c4ae4e6575",
      "statement": "The server entrypoint loads config, initializes the logger, then constructs three independent ZeroHub instances (zeroHubStatic, zeroHubRandom, zeroHubIP) via a shared newZeroHubOrPanic constructor that panics on construction failure, and passes them to the handler, so each hub mode has an isolated hub registry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/cmd/server.go#L25-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:318897bae9dcb784e43f0c6bdd4586199ab1323063572b90d44ad24283129f73:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/cmd/server.go#L41-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ce846692ec81b69018df9f46f75a09a401bb4343180001a23d1fba58ea5e5d8b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_11d056afeae2482eb5555e3341dce77f",
      "statement": "Server configuration is loaded from .env via godotenv and unmarshaled with go-env; key vars are APP_ENVIRONMENT (default dev), APP_HOST (default 0.0.0.0), APP_PORT (default 8080), APP_CLIENT_SECRET (required), APP_HUB_STORAGE/APP_PEER_STORAGE (default memory), APP_TRUST_PROXY (default false), and APP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS (optional comma-separated WebSocket origin allow-list).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/config/config.go#L27-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d34de20c4cbb0894574fdc50f2b71a2fd616e53d0e917c51088a349bba641e0e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a640bf52ab174bd5b1f73e249412edf5",
      "statement": "handler.NewHandler refuses to start when APP_CLIENT_SECRET is empty, because the admin endpoint would otherwise be open to unauthenticated requests.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/handler.go#L148-L155",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d66dd4fd1d6e3a3e13cde31ca521034550027bb330daec0d2c5e42833caae1e0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c946b125db0f4af0b34cfffeef5d5f23",
      "statement": "ZeroHub.GetOrCreateHub and CreateHubIfAbsent share the getOrCreateHubLocked read-then-write under a sync.Mutex so concurrent create and join-or-create calls for the same hub ID collapse to a single hub instead of orphaning one; GetOrCreateHub returns a created flag so callers can decide whether rolling the hub back on a failed upgrade is safe.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/zerohub/zerohub.go#L92-L134",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1c5979890876446b00ca50720c1706501c266777c41140f53965e7e763fd2475:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_973b6aefbd374b2793b3dbf5ba1a17ff",
      "statement": "hub.AddPeer assigns a peer a monotonic numeric ID from an atomic counter, marshals the join signal before registering the peer in PeerStorage (so a marshal failure is a no-op and never leaves a half-registered peer), rejects the join once the hub's closing flag is set, then stores it in PeerStorage, broadcasts a PeerJoinedMessage to the other peers, and sends the new peer a HubInfoMessage.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/hub/hub.go#L99-L171",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f26e757f59106578f4cd70f5aeeae01afefe70d76a9a54f34fe534f63b7b274c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_87b7649845d342a2a742287bdf02fff4",
      "statement": "Hub teardown runs in two places in handler.Upgrade: the socket close handler (peer.Close() plus hub.RemovePeerIfLast(peer.GetId(), zh.HubStore())) and a fallback right after hub.HandleMessage returns. Both call the idempotent RemovePeerIfLast, which removes the peer and deletes the hub from storage only when it was the last peer and the hub is not permanent; a duplicate removal is a no-op that broadcasts nothing, so the PeerDisconnectedMessage and hub deletion are never doubled. A keepalive goroutine pings the peer every idleTimeout/4, closes the socket after WSIdleTimeout (60s) of inactivity, and is joined before the upgrade callback returns so fasthttp can safely recycle the hijacked connection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/config/consts.go#L22-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:441239b22399667f13c57c7f83df67211a956721f3abb2bbf69b9cec6af864ba:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/websocket.go#L145-L234",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:143343642877147119e8ebcd2fcc4e5efe1e5eff8e45be88bcd39538858c36aa:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/hub/hub.go#L181-L205",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:39aa727602e995f2f317ffda6c8ed770a8cc4af731e0dc2a57bc028f029cbd0b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4df69d732b3049588880a9ea4bfaf548",
      "statement": "The server applies an in-package token-bucket rate limiter (rateLimitMiddleware in pkg/handler/ratelimit.go) at 60 requests/minute with continuous refill, answering 429 to excess requests; keys idle longer than 2 minutes are reclaimed by a sweep running at most every 32s. It is keyed by the socket peer address (IP:port, unspoofable) by default, or by the outermost X-Forwarded-For IP only when APP_TRUST_PROXY is set (which must only be enabled behind a proxy that strips or replaces that header). The separate clientIP() helper, which drops the port so all connections from one client IP share a hub, derives the hub ID for IP-keyed hubs, so behind a trusted proxy the IP-hub ID tracks the real client IP rather than the proxy socket address.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/handler.go#L182-L189",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c4e56f386d1c521e11482d38fc4557c8fa6b1a2cdd0ccf761abc052c9dfba8e4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/join_or_create_hub_ip.go#L30-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4ae5c804ecf78475ef832fd685c17821712b5de308927e781537ed0ff855f151:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/ratelimit.go#L10-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:707c423dbd277e37948aa356f9bcc92b5b062c7dced667099ae51b6619ea35a4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/ratelimit.go#L118-L137",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c743f4676502e759ac32ab6ad396869b6ac90cd4df6163c9055507f9983a4a20:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_91ae4835b8e64652b68f503c4c27458e",
      "statement": "Zero-downtime migration: an authenticated /v1/admin/migrate?host=<new> call first validates the host with validateBackupHost (a bare host or host:port, rejecting any scheme, //, path, query, fragment, userinfo, or out-of-range port with a 400 without touching state), then sets backupHost under a read-write mutex and atomically flips isMigrating; while migrating, create/join-or-create requests are rejected via ForwardMigrate, which upgrades the connection and sends a going-away close (code 1001) whose reason is the backup host so clients reconnect to the new host.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/migrate.go#L27-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3569e4eec58a3ed64c2b3fae48fed00aecb6a23f180dff50ecb2d4934ec1a5ed:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/migrate.go#L60-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0a2e77926d565d11ac7b7f645746d736e1f30b28db3d3a6b3b93564d7d2ab1ab:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_379d28f9a4504ca69894f2b9f180016c",
      "statement": "Storage backends are selected by config: MemoryStorage is a mutex-guarded map, and GacheStorage wraps a ntsd/gache/v2 Gache instance with the expired hook disabled and the default TTL overridden to gache.NoTTL so hub and peer entries live until the application removes them explicitly rather than expiring after the 30s default that gache applies to every Set.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/storage/gache.go#L17-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8d0d9a5a7efe85785e3a97c12ed73a123d0fc9975d8d3f3d681b2c12433f8cd9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5cbe6bd3cd134d1d833ce0a9aa9c3e10",
      "statement": "hub.RemovePeerIfLast checks PeerStorage.Get(id) first and is a no-op for a missing peer; for a present peer it deletes the entry under the hub's peer-mutation lock, broadcasts the disconnect signal to all other peers, and deletes the hub from the provided hubStorage when the peer was the last one and the hub is not permanent. TestRemovePeerIfLastIdempotent and TestRemovePeerIfLastLastPeerTwice pin this duplicate-teardown behavior.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/hub/hub.go#L181-L249",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e8d3750a08fae50073d932a233ef6a8da3ba54eea741a19fcbbf75fb7e761dde:"
