        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b7c8cd3abfc340d18ae8650a7ca05b08",
      "statement": "CheckAdminAuth compares the base64-decoded Authorization header against APP_CLIENT_SECRET using crypto/subtle.ConstantTimeCompare, which closes the timing side-channel that a plain non-constant-time string comparison would leave open; on failure it writes a 401 JSON body and returns errAdminUnauthorized so callers perform no state mutation after an auth failure.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/auth.go#L21-L37",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a4d74db698e91b21b5eb155d53b100686436a9a27e1fcf46a0bca823190fdaca:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b250964785404c4591fbca79f764bdd7",
      "statement": "/v1/status is a public read-only health and migration endpoint that answers with a static Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * plus Vary: Origin, a constant rather than a reflection of the request Origin header, because reflecting an arbitrary origin is the classic CORS anti-pattern and is unnecessary when the endpoint is open to all origins; the exposed status and backupHost data is considered public.",
