    {
      "id": "claim_8419e00d1be14a278561a44dd1eeae16",
      "statement": "When the WebSocket upgrade does not fully succeed (a handshake error, or the up-front peerMetadata rejection that already wrote a 400/413 with responseWritten=true) AddPeer never ran, so the hub holds no peer for this request and is empty; CreateHubByID and JoinOrCreateHubByID therefore pass a rollback to the shared finishUpgradeFailure epilogue that calls zh.RemoveHubById on that hub to prevent an unbounded empty-hub leak on memory storage. JoinOrCreateHubByID removes the hub only when this call created it, since a pre-existing hub may hold live peers, and when responseWritten is true the already-written 400/413 is returned as nil instead of being overwritten by a 500.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/create_hub_by_id.go#L14-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f9cfa8543d7c9753a3cfb444706bbf06cf99fb4cb1b1c9597ae4768ebb610243:"
